		<Placemark>
			<name>2955 Shattuck Ave · 74 units · In Review</name>
			<visibility>0</visibility>
			<description><![CDATA[<b>2955 SHATTUCK Ave</b><br/><b>Units:</b> 74<br/><b>VLI Units:</b> 0<br/><b>Stories:</b> 8<br/><b>Height:</b> 25.9m<br/><b>Status:</b> Under Construction<br/><i>Footprint 15,610 sf and height 8 storeys from the project's own Tabulation Form 1.E (2025-05-25), PROPOSED column: lot 16,968 sf x 92% coverage. CORRECTS AN EARLIER EDIT OF MINE THAT TOOK THE EXISTING COLUMN (51% -> 8,654 sf) from a plan set, when a 1.E was on R2 all along. The units row settles the column order beyond doubt: 0 existing, 74 proposed. Before either edit the polygon was a degenerate 1,113 sf sliver. Lot 16,968 sf exceeds the single county parcel (12,207 sf), so this is a multi-parcel site and the extent is approximate; area and height are the architect's own. Moved 1.84 m EAST 2026-08-26: the footprint's WEST edge (its Shattuck frontage — 2955 is on the EAST side of the street) overhung the property line into the roadway. Site is TWO parcels, 53-1589-18-1 (2925 Shattuck, 12,235 sf) + 53-1589-19 (2921 Shattuck, 4,831 sf) = 17,066 sf against the 1.E's stated 16,968 sf lot; at 92% coverage the building nearly fills the site, so placement error shows up immediately as a street intrusion.</i><br/><i>Footprint 15,611 sf and 8 storeys / 85 ft from the Tabulation Form 1.E, PROPOSED column. Read INDEPENDENTLY by two sessions and agreeing; column identified by the form's dwelling-units row. Was 15,611 sf at 28.0 m. 2026-08-26.</i>]]></description>
